In article <19098@castle.ed.ac.uk> philipm@castle.ed.ac.uk (P MacFarlane)
writes:

> What is a polypile?

 A large group of objects, normally armour, crap wands, etc, which a
totally sad person with a wand of polymorph (or, indeed, spell of polymorph)
hopes to change into lots of really useful items. e.g. Like, watch that
useless piece of chainmail become a slightly more useful polished silver
shield...

 If you're abusing it to the max, you kill a load of soldiers (or insert group
of monsters which carry loads of items here) and pile all their equipment into
one big heap.

 I reckon polymorph should only work on monsters to make them easier to kill
(perhaps...) and corpses to provide useful items (as presently happens with
dragons...).

 People who want to polypile might as well just play in wizard mode and
save themselves the bother.

 Flames to you know where...

